/-!
# Exact nonsingular quotient rows outside the box container

The sixteen binary subspaces in each of the three whole source images are
checked by thirteen native conjugators. Every subgroup containing the original
pair either maps into Figure 2(a), or maps ONTO (b), (c), (d), (c′), or (d′).
Forward and reverse generator identities certify equality in the latter cases.
All proper subgroups of (b) extend into a conjugate of (a), so (b′) needs no
separate branch at this quotient boundary. The actual seed pair and Figure 1
permutation are preserved by every conjugator.

`elementary_container_exact_rows` combines this proper-subgroup analysis with
the exhaustive Sylow placement. `ExactSource` applies the conclusion through
the literal ambient quotient; no geometric source callback is assumed.
Source: Kleidman--Wilson, *The Maximal Subgroups of J4* (1988), Lemma 2.3.1,
printed p.492. Native coordinates and word attribution are inherited from the
Figure 2 source generators and the ATLAS star generators.
-/

